.TH LUGH-NODE 8 "2026-11-23" "Lugh 0.6.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lugh-node \- the directory and single sign-on service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lugh-node
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B lugh-node init
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lugh-node
holds the identities of people and services, signs them in with a password and a second
factor, and answers who someone is and what they may do: OAuth 2 and OpenID Connect for
applications, a management API and dashboard for administrators, and LDAP. It listens with
TLS 1.3 only.
.PP
With no command it serves. It is normally run by
.BR systemd (1)
as
.BR lugh.service ,
installed disabled.
.PP
.B lugh-node init
makes this node's keyring in the state directory and writes a new master key, 32 raw bytes,
to standard output, which must not be a terminal. Pipe it to
.B systemd-creds encrypt \-\-name=lugh-master-key \- /etc/credstore.encrypted/lugh-master-key
and the unit loads it as the credential lugh-master-key. On the first node, init is the
genesis: it also makes the user root, in the group administrators, and shows root's password
once. Init never replaces a keyring.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
The configuration to read.
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase
With init: derive the master key from a typed passphrase, for a host without systemd
credentials; every start then asks for it.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and every setting, and exit.
.SH SETTINGS
Each setting comes from the configuration file, its environment variable or its flag; each
overrides the one before, after the defaults and
.I secrets.yaml
beside the configuration.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " \fIlevel\fR"
log.level: all, debug, info, warn or error (LUGH_LOG_LEVEL).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-format " \fIformat\fR"
log.format: text or json (LUGH_LOG_FORMAT).
.TP
.BR \-\-server\-address " \fIaddress\fR"
server.address: the IP address to listen on (LUGH_SERVER_ADDRESS).
.TP
.BR \-\-server\-port " \fIport\fR"
server.port (LUGH_SERVER_PORT).
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-certificate " \fIpath\fR", " \-\-tls\-key " \fIpath\fR"
tls.certificate and tls.key (LUGH_TLS_CERTIFICATE, LUGH_TLS_KEY).
.TP
.BR \-\-state\-directory " \fIpath\fR"
state.directory: the keyring and the store (LUGH_STATE_DIRECTORY).
.TP
.BR \-\-static\-directory " \fIpath\fR"
static.directory: the dashboard's files (LUGH_STATIC_DIRECTORY).
.TP
.BR \-\-oauth\-issuer " \fIurl\fR"
oauth.issuer: the https URL clients reach Lugh at (LUGH_OAUTH_ISSUER).
.TP
.BR \-\-oauth\-mtls\-port " \fIport\fR"
oauth.mtls_port: a listener that asks for client certificates, or 0 for none
(LUGH_OAUTH_MTLS_PORT).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/lugh/config.yaml
The configuration, read when neither \-\-config nor LUGH_CONFIG names one.
.TP
.I /etc/lugh/secrets.yaml
Secrets, in the configuration's shape.
.TP
.I /etc/lugh/tls/cert.pem\fR, \fI/etc/lugh/tls/key.pem
The node's certificate pair.
.TP
.I /var/lib/lugh
The keyring and the store.
.TP
.I /etc/credstore.encrypted/lugh-master-key
The sealed master key.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-creds (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/lugh/architecture.md.gz
